.claude/worktrees/
# macOS / iCloud Drive sync conflicts. The repository lives under ~/Documents, which iCloud
# syncs by default, and a conflict is written beside the original as "schema 2.toml" rather
# than announced. Thirty-five appeared on 4 Sep — stale copies of tracked files, all of them
# older versions whose content was already in git history.
#
# They are ignored rather than merely deleted because the failure mode is silent and expensive:
# `contracts/v1/tests` was being collected twice, so a suite reporting 801 tests was really
# running 568, and a `git add -A` would have committed the lot.
*\ [0-9].*
*\ [0-9][0-9].*
.DS_Store

# Local development secrets — the bot password, and anything else that is a credential rather
# than a domain parameter. `config/quant_arena.toml` is committed and hashed and holds neither
# (config/settings.py, and the 2026-08-31 configuration/infrastructure split); docker-compose.yml
# gives QA_BOT_PASSWORD deliberately no default, "because a password with a default is a password
# in the repository the first time someone forgets to set it". Keeping the file untracked is what
# makes that true while still leaving the value somewhere findable on this machine.
secrets-local.txt

# Claude Code local permission rules. Personal to this machine — the allow/ask/deny lists name
# local commands and this checkout, and they are not a team-wide agreement. Project-wide rules
# would go in .claude/settings.json, which IS committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
